2. Verify that the homepage contains the Facebook logo, search bar, and login/register buttons.
3. Expected Result: The homepage should display the expected UI elements.

2 | Pre-login scenario: Homepage field validations | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Enter invalid email address in the search bar
3. Click on the search button
4. Verify that an error message is displayed indicating "Invalid email or phone number".
5. Expected Result: The error message should be displayed.

3 | Pre-login scenario: Homepage field validations | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Enter valid email address in the search bar
3. Click on the search button
4. Verify that a dropdown list of suggested users is displayed.
5. Expected Result: The dropdown list should be displayed.

4 | Positive login flow | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Click on the "Log In" button
3. Enter valid email address and password
4. Click on the "Log In" button
5. Verify that the user is logged in successfully.
6. Expected Result: The user should be logged in.

5 | Negative login scenario: Invalid email | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Click on the "Log In" button
3. Enter invalid email address and valid password
4. Click on the "Log In" button
5. Verify that an error message is displayed indicating "Invalid email or phone number".
6. Expected Result: The error message should be displayed.

6 | Negative login scenario: Invalid password | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Click on the "Log In" button
3. Enter valid email address and invalid password
4. Click on the "Log In" button
5. Verify that an error message is displayed indicating "Invalid email or phone number".
6. Expected Result: The error message should be displayed.

7 | Negative login scenario: Empty fields | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Click on the "Log In" button
3. Leave both email and password fields empty
4. Click on the "Log In" button
5. Verify that an error message is displayed indicating "The email or phone number you entered doesn't match any account".
6. Expected Result: The error message should be displayed.

8 | Error messages | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Enter invalid email address and valid password
3. Click on the "Log In" button
4. Verify that an error message is displayed indicating "Invalid email or phone number".
5. Expected Result: The error message should be displayed.

9 | Navigation after login | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Log in with valid credentials
3. Verify that the user can navigate to their profile page.
4. Expected Result: The user should be able to navigate to their profile page.

10 | Logout behavior | 
1. Open https://www.facebook.com/
2. Log in with valid credentials
3. Click on the "Log Out" button
4. Verify that the user is logged out successfully.
5. Expected Result: The user should be logged out.
